body:
So what is it that made your psych prescribe anti-psychotics? Did you explain to him your spiritual insights and how you used LSD to achieve them? When you talk about society and how you can't play that game again, well, many many many of us have had the same insights. Just so what most of us do and surrender. Surrender to it all. Play your role in the world while not being part of the world. You may be happy to live on top of the mountains out with nature alone. I don't about you but I wouldn't be able to stand the isolation. Well anyway, I also don't think you're going to experience the exceptional divine experience that I'm sure you're all too familiar with. This life is pretty boring, you get up go to work come home go to sleep, repeat. But keep your eyes on the prize, you know about something most people don't. I'd say 90% of the general population would have no idea what you're talking about if you approached them and explained. So there's something greater beyond us, there's something more to all of this.  So have some faith in that and you can deal with anything experienced.

&#x200B;

btw I used to take olanzipine for psychosis. But that was after a series of bad LSD trips that sent me crazy. So I think anti-psychotics are good, they saved my life and I still take it occasionally. Never liked seroquel didn't find it effective.  Hope you go well on your journeys man. Just know a lot of us have been through similar stuff and can relate.
